// expect: 7
// A STATE ELEMENT'S INIT IS DISCARDED. `accumulate(5)` declares a register
// whose prior starts at five; the recurrence adds each tick's input to the
// prior, so two ticks of 1 answer 6, then 7. The program answers 2 — the
// register starts at zero, exactly as if `accumulate(0)` had been written —
// with no diagnostic (measured 2026-09-23).
//
// Why: the `<~` state element is read by the compiler for its DEPTH alone
// (feedback_depth in infer.mn), and the line's globals are declared at zero.
// Nothing reads the init, and until the landing that banked this fixture the
// spec was also lowered as a value that every pre-pass walked and the emit
// then dropped, so the init was carried through the whole back end and still
// never arrived. The contract is the surface's own answer; it retires when
// the site reads the init as it reads the depth and the register is born
// holding it (Hβ.dataflow.state-element-is-read-whole).
fn step(x) -> Int = ((prev) => x + prev) <~ accumulate(5)

fn main() -> Int = {
  let a = step(1)
  step(1)
}
